# Copy to .env.local for development. .env* is gitignored — never commit real values.

# Supabase project (Settings -> API). The anon key is PUBLIC by design: it ships
# in the JS bundle, and RLS is what protects the data. Rotating it is easy;
# relying on it for secrecy is not.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# KILL SWITCH: leave VITE_SUPABASE_URL empty to disable the backend entirely.
# The app then degrades to its pre-Supabase behaviour — localStorage plus manual
# CSV/JSON download — with the sign-in screen bypassed. One env var + a redeploy
# is the ~90s rollback if Supabase misbehaves mid-round.

# clinician | dev
#   clinician -> compiles out Reveal arms, Start over, and the arm key itself
#   dev       -> keeps every affordance (the default for local work)
VITE_APP_MODE=dev

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ⛔ NEVER PUT THESE HERE — every VITE_* value is compiled into the public bundle:
#     RESEND_API_KEY            -> supabase secrets set RESEND_API_KEY=...
#     SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY -> your shell, for the duration of one command
# Both are server-side secrets. A key in this file ships to every visitor.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT a Vite variable. The service-role key bypasses RLS and is a full-database
# credential — it must never appear in .env, the bundle, or CI. Export it in
# your shell only for the length of a seed run:
#   export SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=...
#   python3 scripts/data/seed_batch.py
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
